      "ticket": "8e5db5f3edb2",
      "note": "KICKED BACK BY THE CLEARANCE GATE, and the finding is about this voyage's RECORD, not its code.\n\nThe PROVED gate refused twice, naming `proof_declares_the_ticket` against\ntest_chart_verdict.py and test_falsifier_verdict.py. Both refusals are correct and neither\nis about the build. On the PROVEME crossing of 2026-09-11T09:51:47 I put those two proofs in\n`also_proven_by` because criterion 6 of the claiming validate berth runs them as a REGRESSION\ncheck — they must stay green under this change, and they did (38 passed). But `also_proven_by`\nis not the field for \"proofs this voyage ran\"; the coverage rung reads it as \"proofs that\nCOVER this boat\", and asks each one for a PROVES entry naming this ticket. Neither has one,\nand neither should: this ticket's five falsifier clauses are all about write_verdict /\ninspect_verdict, and those two proofs answer other tickets' clauses about the same machine.\nInventing PROVES entries to satisfy the gate would be manufacturing coverage, which is the\nexact shape Law 8 calls worse than a red — so the record is what gets corrected, not the proofs.\n\nWHY THE RETREAT GOES PAST BUILDME AND NOT TO IT. The journal is append-only (Law 7): the\n09:51:47 record cannot be edited, and nothing in the grammar erases a crossing — a disposition\nis an ejection, not a correction. The one eraser that exists is the cut in\n`crossings.proven_by_since_buildme`, which unions the proofs named at or after the LATEST\nFORWARD BUILDME crossing, and whose docstring calls that cut \"the WHOLE of the kick-back\nprotection ... what keeps that union from also picking up the abandoned proof of a build that\nwas kicked back.\" This is that case, arriving on the mechanism built for it. A back edge TO\nBUILDME would not do it — the cut keys on a FORWARD BUILDME entry — so the retreat lands at\nTICKETME and the build re-crosses, which is also the honest severity: the ticket is being\nre-taken, the code is not being rewritten.\n\nNOTHING IN THE TREE CHANGES ON THIS RETREAT. No source file is touched, no proof is re-run for\na different answer, no seal moves. The re-crossed BUILDME names only\ntest_the_instrument_is_run.py, which does cover the boat: the coverage rung's clause check\nalready passes on it alone (the two `proof_declares_the_ticket` entries were the ONLY lacks\nleft once the hollow evidence sealed), so all five falsifier clauses have teeth in that one\nproof and the neighbours were surplus the whole time.\n\nTHE FINDING WORTH KEEPING, and it is about the chart leg, not the builder: nothing at the\nPROVEME crossing tells a builder that `also_proven_by` is a COVERAGE claim rather than a record\nof what was run. The field name reads like the second thing. The gate catches it — four\ncrossings later, after a hollow seal and two refusals — which is the right place to catch it\nand an expensive place to learn it.",
